landing-review: landing 10b (structure-shadow pair gated), FIVE dedicated read-only rounds at high, 2026-09-18.

Reviewed range grew with the landing; round 4 read the whole of main...2b1e643 with fresh eyes.

R1  10 findings. Gate raised before nine early returns; it asked 'is the pass
    armed' not 'will anything paint it'; a VirtualProtect-failure stub leak; the
    claim that tagpu_overlay_draw calls the publisher unconditionally (false --
    four gates above it), which motivated the 8-frame watchdog.
R2  HIGH x2. 'classicpp_on() || posedraw_live()' treats the two painters as
    alternatives; both come out of pdu[] and need tagpu_posedraw_ready(), so with
    the posed program refused the gate stood raised over an empty frame in the
    SHIPPED DEFAULT. And the Vulkan lane does not paint the slant via
    tagpu_shadow_handover -- begin/end are called only below the !gl_draws return.
R3  HIGH. mapLive observes the CASTER pass, not a RECEIVER: with nterr == 0 the
    map is built, nothing samples it, every structure loses its shadow. Fixed by
    quoting the consumer's own predicate.
R4  No HIGH in the code -- stubs decoded byte-for-byte against the pristine image,
    incoming-branch scan re-run from scratch, install/rollback/watchdog all sound.
    Two HIGH in the claims: 'no picture is possible' was false (the composite
    DISCARDS our fragment where the surface is not the key, so the engine's pixels
    reach the screen), and renderer=gdi is not stock -- tagpu_apply_patches applies
    THREE unconditional patches, and the tagpu_curs pair changes input semantics.
R5  No HIGH in the code. Two MEDIUM, both about the fix R4 prompted: the key-fill
    term was published a frame late, giving up to two teal frames on every terrown
    acquisition; and npdSlant > 0 was self-referential (units[i].shadow IS the
    gate), a bistable latch. Both fixed: terrown now raises the gate itself,
    before publishing its own skip byte.

MEASURED, renderer=openglcore, shadow-struct, camera [1600,1600]:
  engine's restored slant inside a key-filled viewport = 8779 px of (0,128,128),
  four opaque teal blobs on four structures. After the fix: 0. After the rework: 0.
  The gate's raise is an ordering (both stores render-thread, x86 store-store),
  confirmed in the log: owndraw SKIPPED prints before terrown SKIPPED at entry.

ALSO MEASURED, and it invalidates a method this repo was using: two captures of
the SAME build, fixture, camera and configuration across two boots differ by
421720 px (54% of frame, mean delta 3.5) because the Classic++ restorer's reveal
is never at the same point twice. Cross-boot PIXEL counts measure nothing here;
the exact colour count is what carries the result.

Not covered: the renderer=gdi picture (landing 10c); gdi is stock with respect to
structure shadows only, not as a lane; single fixture, one camera, one gate-down
state.
